            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> > how a plugin should restore its state when sessions are restored\n> \n> My first reaction is \"they shouldn't\"\n\nTo clarify: plugins shouldn't try to restore *internal state*. That is just a recipe for misery.\n\nHowever, if a plugin provides URI buffers (such as `fugitive://`), they should actually support that. That is one of the implied purposes of URIs: to be able to navigate to them in a content-addressable manner.",
