            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "> Yes, anything that can be treated as \"data\" stored in `stdpath('data')` is certainly a candidate for restoring.\n\nGood to hear. We've been storing nvim-tree bookmarks at `stdpath(\"data\") .. \"/nvim-tree-bookmarks.json\"`\n\n> Plugins are free to do whatever they want, but as general guidance we shouldn't set the expectation that plugins should try to maintain all of their internal state and restore it after a session. They will be full of bugs, and it makes sessions worse, not better.\n\nGreat care will be taken in the future and we'll try to keep to a minimum.",
